test(tenant): expand jail coverage to 18 cases

Roadmap item 13 continuation — thicken the tenant jail suite to
match handshake (12) + snapshot-crypto (13) coverage levels.

+8 cases (10 -> 18):
  - empty string resolves to USERSPACE_ROOT itself (boundary)
  - nested traversal "a/b/../../../etc/passwd" rejected
  - redundant-slash normalization "uploads///a.png"
  - dotted segments "uploads/./a.png" flattened
  - null byte at start of path rejected
  - null byte at end of path rejected
  - tenantInfo() exposes app/userspace/dataRoot + machine-id
  - app jail rejects userspace-style traversal

Why these specifically: the jail is the single most security-load-bearing
function in tenant.ts. Any path-handling regression silently allows
arbitrary FS read/write from a customer admin upload. Test cases
mirror real exploit shapes (encoded traversal, embedded nulls, multi-slash).

Total lib tests now 88/0 (was 80/0).
Build: 510 modules.